            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Isn't checking for `#vim.api.nvim_buf_get_extmarks(0, mc, 0, -1, { limit = 1 }) > 0` enough?\n\nBut besides that, the ability to check whether the operator is performing with multicursor active is a bit orthogonal to the issue. The problem here is that there is no way to fully replicate the workflow *if* multicursor or `:h edit-repeat` is active. Resolving user input during expression mapping restrictions has issues. If there were none, I don't think checking for active multicursor is even needed.",
