            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> As resolving the keys during expression mapping is not the full proof approach,\n\n`lhs` is also not foolproof. if it were then there would be no debate. \n\nwe need to try to see what the limits are for resolving a reliable \"RHS\". LHS is an option that's available (and easy to switch to) once we have exhausted the limits of RHS. and discovering those limits improves the system in general. there's no rush.",
