            "body": "> > One solution that (currently) works here is to resolve user input _during expression mapping evaluation_ (i.e. before returning `g@l`). **However**, it hits `:h map-expression` limitations (textlock in current and other buffers, etc.).\n> \n> I think lifting these restrictions will be easy.\n\n[Unfortunately, there is also a case of a true operator (action that asks for textobject) that can not benefit from resolving user input during expression mapping](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41657#issuecomment-5542956936).",
